{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Look down from Your holy dwelling, etc.</b> Since it says above: 'I have done according to all that You commanded me,' Rashi explained: I rejoiced and I caused others to rejoice. Therefore, 'Look down from מְעוֹן' — just as we say 'that the joy is in His dwelling,' and from there may You return and gladden him. And in tractate Ḥagigah (12b) they said: מָעוֹן — in it are ranks of ministering angels who recite song by night and are silent by day because of the glory of Israel, as it says (Psalms 42:9): 'By day HaShem will command His lovingkindness, and in the night His song is with me,' and Rashi explained: 'By day HaShem will command His lovingkindness' — He commands the angels to be silent, so as to perform kindness for those in need of kindness, and these are the lower ones — thus far his language. Now, it is plausible to hear that the Holy One, blessed be He, performs this kindness in the merit of the kindness that the lower ones do with one another, and the tithe is included in kindness. Therefore he says: in the merit of the kindness that I performed with this tithe for those in need of kindness, 'Look down from מְעוֹן' to perform kindness for those in need of kindness — for those heavens whose name is 'מָעוֹן' are uniquely designated for this and uniquely designated for joy, for where there is joy there is song, but not in a place where there is no joy. And further, in the merit of 'I have not transgressed Your commandments' — from the language of אֵין מַעֲבִירִין עַל הַמִּצְוֹת (one does not pass over commandments), that I did not pass over from one commandment to give precedence to what is later — so too 'Look down from Your holy dwelling (מְעוֹן)' not to give precedence to what is later, for indeed the thought of Israel preceded the world, and they are earlier even than the angels. Therefore it is fitting that the angels should not say song until Israel say first by day, and afterward the angels by night, as it is written (Deuteronomy 33:27): 'מְעֹנָה אֱלֹהֵי קֶדֶם' — that is, the Elohim of Israel who are earlier — 'and from beneath' — these are the angels, who are called 'זְרֹעוֹת עוֹלָם' (everlasting arms), for in מָעוֹן Israel precede, as stated. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Tanhuma Tissa 14): every הַשְׁקָפָה (looking down) is for evil, except for the gift to the poor, which transforms wrath to compassion — and this is in the merit of the trait of compassion in man, which transforms the trait of cruelty within him to compassion; so too the Holy One, blessed be He, transforms wrath to compassion."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:14:04.724187539Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}